# NETMAP FULL — example environment file. COPY to .env and fill in YOUR OWN keys.
# NEVER commit a real .env file, and NEVER paste a real key into chat, a repo,
# or this browser demo's key field if you do not want it stored locally.
# This browser demo does not read .env and does not call real APIs:
# adapters return mock data even when a key flag is set locally.
# A future server version would read these variables and call ONLY APIs
# the owner is authorised to use, for inventory/CMDB/cloud data — never
# for unauthenticated scanning of networks you do not own.

# CMDB / inventory export API (future server version only)
CMDB_API_URL=https://example-inventory.internal/api/v1/assets
CMDB_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Cloud inventory API (future server version only)
CLOUD_API_URL=https://example-cloud.internal/api/v1/instances
CLOUD_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Generic inventory / agent export API (future server version only)
INVENTORY_API_URL=https://example-inventory.internal/api/v1/devices
INVENTORY_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE

# How to add keys later (server version):
# 1. cp .env.example .env
# 2. Edit .env with your keys (keep .env out of git — see .gitignore guidance in README).
# 3. Restart the server adapter; the adapter names (cmdb / inventory / cloud)
#    stay the same, only the data source changes from mock to authorised API.
